# T09 sink-side recv_done_trigger on a regular P2P flow
# Regression test for the previously-latent upstream bug: a
# UecSink's _end_trigger was stored but never fired. Now,
# set_expected_bytes (set by main_uec.cpp when recv_done_trigger is
# present) plus a byte-count check in UecSink::receivePacket makes
# the named trigger actually fire when the last byte arrives,
# letting a downstream P2P flow start.
# Expect:
#   - no BCAST_COMPLETE lines (pure P2P)
#   - "Trigger 1 fired, 1 targets" (the named oneshot activates
#      the waiting flow id 2)
#   - both P2P endpoints constructed (log names uec_5_10 and uec_2_3)
Nodes 16
Connections 2
Triggers 1
5->10 id 1 start 0 size 4096 recv_done_trigger 1
2->3 id 2 trigger 1 size 4096
trigger id 1 oneshot
